Local changes from upstream (PassiveLAB sub-phase 1.4.1):
- modules/util_gds_reader.py, modules/util_meshlines.py, modules/util_simulation_setup.py:
  converted intra-package `import util_x` statements to relative imports (`from . import util_x`)
  so the modules work as a proper Python package under
  `passivelab.characterization.openems.vendor.modules` instead of relying on being added to
  `sys.path` individually.
- modules/util_simulation_setup.py: `runSimulation()` gained an explicit `interactive_preview:
  bool = False` parameter gating the AppCSXCAD GUI-preview launch, replacing the implicit
  `if 1 in excite_portnumbers:` condition. Upstream code (and the golden notebook it was copied
  from) relied on a one-line source edit to disable this for headless/batch runs; this vendored
  copy makes that an explicit, tested parameter instead. No other behavioral changes.
